            ("You", "よく写真を撮りに出かけます。カメラが趣味なんです。", "Yoku shashin o tori ni dekakemasu. Kamera ga shumi nan desu.", "I often go out to take photos. Photography is my hobby."),
            ("Kenta", "へえ、どんな写真を撮るんですか。", "Hee, donna shashin o torun desu ka.", "Oh, what kind of photos do you take?"),
            ("You", "町の風景が多いです。特に、夜の東京が好きです。", "Machi no fuukei ga ooi desu. Toku ni, yoru no Toukyou ga suki desu.", "Mostly cityscapes. I especially love Tokyo at night."),
            ("Kenta", "見てみたいです。", "Mite mitai desu.", "I'd love to see them."),
            ("You", "これは先週、渋谷で撮りました。", "Kore wa senshuu, Shibuya de torimashita.", "I took this one in Shibuya last week."),
            ("Kenta", "きれい！プロみたいですね。", "Kirei! Puro mitai desu ne.", "Beautiful! You're like a pro."),
            ("You", "ありがとうございます。ケンタさんの趣味は何ですか。", "Arigatou gozaimasu. Kenta-san no shumi wa nan desu ka.", "Thanks. What are your hobbies, Kenta?"),
            ("Kenta", "僕は料理とサッカーです。", "Boku wa ryouri to sakkaa desu.", "Cooking and soccer."),
            ("You", "サッカーは、するほうですか、見るほうですか。", "Sakkaa wa, suru hou desu ka, miru hou desu ka.", "Do you play soccer or watch it?"),
            ("Kenta", "両方です。毎週日曜日に、会社のチームで試合をしています。", "Ryouhou desu. Maishuu nichiyoubi ni, kaisha no chiimu de shiai o shite imasu.", "Both. Every Sunday I play matches with the company team."),
            ("You", "すごいですね。ポジションはどこですか。", "Sugoi desu ne. Pojishon wa doko desu ka.", "Cool. What position do you play?"),
            ("Kenta", "ディフェンダーです。あまり上手じゃないですけどね。", "Difendaa desu. Amari jouzu ja nai desu kedo ne.", "Defender. I'm not very good, though."),
            ("You", "料理は、どんなものを作りますか。", "Ryouri wa, donna mono o tsukurimasu ka.", "What kind of food do you cook?"),
            ("Kenta", "最近は、イタリア料理にはまっています。パスタを手作りしているんです。", "Saikin wa, Itaria ryouri ni hamatte imasu. Pasuta o tezukuri shite irun desu.", "Lately I'm hooked on Italian food. I make pasta from scratch."),
            ("You", "パスタを手作り？難しくないですか。", "Pasuta o tezukuri? Muzukashiku nai desu ka.", "Homemade pasta? Isn't that hard?"),
            ("Kenta", "最初は難しかったけど、慣れたら楽しいですよ。", "Saisho wa muzukashikatta kedo, naretara tanoshii desu yo.", "It was hard at first, but once you get the hang of it, it's fun."),
            ("You", "私も料理を習いたいです。日本料理は全然作れないんです。", "Watashi mo ryouri o naraitai desu. Nihon ryouri wa zenzen tsukurenain desu.", "I want to learn to cook too. I can't make Japanese food at all."),
            ("Kenta", "じゃあ、今度うちで一緒に作りませんか。肉じゃがなら簡単ですよ。", "Jaa, kondo uchi de issho ni tsukurimasen ka. Nikujaga nara kantan desu yo.", "Then why don't we cook together at my place sometime? Nikujaga is easy."),
            ("You", "肉じゃがって何ですか。", "Nikujaga tte nan desu ka.", "What's nikujaga?"),
            ("Kenta", "肉とじゃがいもを、甘い醤油で煮た料理です。日本の家庭料理の代表ですね。", "Niku to jagaimo o, amai shouyu de nita ryouri desu. Nihon no katei ryouri no daihyou desu ne.", "Meat and potatoes simmered in sweet soy sauce. It's classic Japanese home cooking."),
            ("You", "おいしそう！ぜひ作りたいです。", "Oishisou! Zehi tsukuritai desu.", "Sounds delicious! I'd love to make it."),
